==Introduction==

===Abstract===

A cryptographically relevant quantum computer (CRQC) poses a threat to a large body of deployed cryptographic protocols.
In particular, it solves the Computational Diffie-Hellman (CDH) problem, so the protocols that use Elliptic Curve Diffie-Hellman (ECDH) key agreement are vulnerable.
Attacks on them are retroactive and typically affect the privacy of their users.
This document specifies '''HKE''', a hybrid key encapsulation that instantiates the UG framework of the CFRG draft [https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/html/draft-irtf-cfrg-hybrid-kems-12 ''Hybrid PQ/T Key Encapsulation Mechanisms''] and derives a 32-byte shared secret <code>K</code> from two components: an ECDH on <code>secp256k1</code> and a post-quantum key-encapsulation mechanism [https://csrc.nist.gov/pubs/fips/203/final <code>ML-KEM-768</code>], combined so that <code>K</code> remains pseudorandom as long as one of the two components is unbroken.

